# Liskov Substitution Principle (LSP)

- Subtypes/implementations must be safely usable anywhere the base contract is expected.
- Do not narrow accepted inputs or strengthen preconditions in implementations.
- Do not weaken guarantees or change expected semantics in overridden behavior.
- Keep error behavior and side effects consistent with interface expectations.

## Review checklist

- Can the new implementation replace existing one without caller changes?
- Are method contracts (inputs/outputs/errors) still honored?
- Are edge-case behaviors compatible with the abstraction?
